, when $|x|=1,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=-1$ and $x=1$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{1}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3/2}}+⋯\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the $p$-series test.  So the endpoint $x=1$ is included in our interval.\n\n- When $x=-1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{{1}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3/2}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3/2}}+⋯\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the alternating series test.  So the endpoint $x=-1$ is included in our interval.\n\nTherefore, the interval of convergence is $[-1,1].$" 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298501 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298502 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298503 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298504 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298505 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1041 "selection" 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298502 13194139534606 true] [17592186298500 1110 #uuid "b35889aa-5974-5f63-ade5-e24dbd1880a5" 13194139534606 true] [17592186298501 1034 "x\\in [-\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{2}{3}]" 13194139534606 true] [17592186298501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534606 true] [17592186298501 1111 #uuid "9af78bdf-be93-5e86-8fd9-42c8223b9d30" 13194139534606 true] [17592186298502 1034 "x\\in [-1,1]" 13194139534606 true] [17592186298502 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534606 true] [17592186298502 1111 #uuid "697ba